{"title":"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:55)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:55)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integer</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e880b118bfa7c5db071a4ed8bb0890168702843f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> denote the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Increasing_sequence\" title=\"Increasing sequence\"> increasing</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_sequence\" title=\"Arithmetic sequence\">arithmetic sequence</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a> whose first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and whose common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.  For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/54147dbf4167d407147e92a3439b0d168c96bee8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence\" title=\"Sequence\">sequence</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3f4b43b9e1d4e8744ccffa6f1640fc8805a53d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,4,7,10,\\ldots.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> For how many values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> does <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e880b118bfa7c5db071a4ed8bb0890168702843f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> contain the term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5b442c275b4324f100c365b774e872b6b21f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th term of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e880b118bfa7c5db071a4ed8bb0890168702843f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5b442c275b4324f100c365b774e872b6b21f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aa03eafb7bf38b5bfbbdc11ba38c7afa7d117b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+(n-1)k=2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f67c74eae8e07353269b05bdd0b674f4034dc8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(n-1)=2004=2^2\\cdot 3\\cdot 167$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"230\" height=\"19\" />.  The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ordered_pair\" title=\"Ordered pair\">ordered pairs</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/11853bdc32f0dd1a10ce5f1a8cf5459d10d7a3ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k,n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> of positive integers that satisfy the last equation are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a068734a097bb7c888cc32661e5879aa7c3adebd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2004)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fbfc6d01239f9ee6c1eba05db7ada7195ed79b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,1002)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/a/0ca83ac10c6b455303b4b9bad34a307650ed7833.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,668)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349d5d6d2457c34058f19d8f2a35fe280a9d2972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,501)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a98d1583eb39762425b29af5721b9d77bd91dfe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,334)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/5/9b5bae70da1c900e8af7094560db54294a330037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(12,167)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce830eb5e569fc55dab2664494e3ae0cb04952ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(167,12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc8102e47ec75421bdec6dd0bebcdfa53b933054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(334,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1ee12ade1f615ce992e8af87bb7191a2acfb3fc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(501,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/b/50baf8869ef429b21cb8a9fe81e3440f322b5735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(668,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1eda868493904cb41df7f4187e1d10dc20afa770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1002,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4da9ce780b545c0b470cdda52c09ab42f3938c9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2004,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, and each of these gives a possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Thus the requested number of values is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/6/f16dcde358a301b519e85db633abdf0fe89f0f2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Alternatively, notice that the formula for the number of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisor\" title=\"Divisor\">divisors</a> states that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ea566618248cc7b1fa88710aa9e7e2e741dc910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 + 1)(1 + 1)(1 + 1) = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" /> divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5b6b6964dba2140920c76382f3d22121f5b44c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2\\cdot 3^1\\cdot 167^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Any term in the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e880b118bfa7c5db071a4ed8bb0890168702843f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> can be written as 1+kx.  If this is to equal 2005, then the remainder when 2005 is divided by k is 1.\n</p><p>Now all we have to do is find the numbers of factors of 2004.  There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ecb80da95aeacb3f23dddce20b85274b0f415a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 + 1)(1 + 1)(1 + 1) = \\boxed{012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"228\" height=\"25\" /> divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5b6b6964dba2140920c76382f3d22121f5b44c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2\\cdot 3^1\\cdot 167^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Note that although the remainder when 2005 divided by 1 is not 1, it still works- <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d5ee88ffc7d59f9c282b366953fb4fa4051f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> would be the sequence of all positive integers, in which 2005 must appear.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:55.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:55)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:55)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:55)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/cRLjTJui0UI\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/cRLjTJui0UI</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p><p>Note: the problem where this is linked is covered 1:45-2:40\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qL0OOYZiaqA?t=83\">https://youtu.be/qL0OOYZiaqA?t=83</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I\" title=\"2005 AIME I\">2005 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2005\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017063203\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 271/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6376/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.650      1 -total\n 65.28%   10.869      1 Template:AIME_box\n 33.45%    5.570      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2655:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017063203 and revision id 292832. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}